litehtml for pages that scripts change: media_changed() styles the whole
tree again from its style sheets, as after parsing, and builds the render
tree again - whether the media changed or not. A script changes classes,
ids, attributes and the tree itself, and the elements' lists of matched
selectors (kept so that only those need checking again) cannot follow
such changes: a class added can make a selector match that never did.
So the lists are dropped and the sheets matched afresh. Nothing in
litehtml calls media_changed(); the browser does, after a script.

